<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 0.94 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 0.94 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 0.72 points, 0.94 percent, to 75.62 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index fell 32.86 points, 0.96 percent, to 3,389.49.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 12.99 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
